agent-power-manager for Debian
===============================

`apm` is a command-line program run by the normal user. It does not install a
service or create a system user.

The package owns `/usr/bin/apm` and its package documentation only. APM keeps
its state under `~/.apm`, its cache under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/apm` or
`~/.cache/apm`, and resources under the configured Agent homes. Both `remove`
and `purge` leave those user-owned paths unchanged. Reinstalling the package
does not reset, migrate, or repair the preserved data.

Run `apm --help` for command usage. The default cloud provider uses HTTPS and
therefore requires the installed `ca-certificates` package.
